# 311: §6 `.35` — the compiler raises NO errors, so an unknown name is a runtime
# error raised when execution REACHES it. Lines 1 and 2 print first and their
# output is part of the result. An engine that resolved names statically would
# produce an empty output plus this error, which is exactly the divergence this
# case exists to catch; it is also what protects the partial-output rule, since
# a static pass would delete prior output for every case in this file.
--- source
print 1;
print 2;
print nope();
--- expect
1
2
error: Name at line 3: undefined function 'nope'
